  - rule-based modeling
  - BNGL
  - PyBNF
abstract: >-
  FluBNF forecasts weekly influenza hospital admissions for the 52 US
  jurisdictions of the CDC FluSight challenge. Its shipped forecast is an
  unfitted, equal-weight, quantile-averaged ensemble of two members: a
  sequential particle filter over an SIHRS compartmental model written in
  BNGL, fitted with a fork of PyBNF on the bngsim engine, and a calendar
  analog whose donor pool excludes the calendar-inverted 2021-22 season.
  In a vintage-true retrospective of the 2023-24, 2024-25 and 2025-26
  seasons at full grid (15,460 scored cells), the production engine in
  this repository scores a pooled weighted interval score of 0.723
  relative to the CDC FluSight-baseline (ratio of WIS sums on shared cells;
  0.834, 0.716 and 0.663 by season), beating the baseline in every season.
  The v1.0.0 release sealed a record of 0.678 (0.813, 0.618, 0.683) on a
  particle filter kernel with an undeclared behaviour that has since been
  corrected; both records and the correction are in docs/RELEASE-1.0.md.
  All scores are self-computed from the hub's archived vintage data and
  baseline files, and are retrospective replays rather than real-time
  submissions.
